# p_4f8d — Marco's Real Commuter Kit: Lunchbox Goes, Vitamins and Journal Stay

The per-object evidence resolves the commuter-kit question. Marco's lunchbox is out of the house during his work shift: the robot made four looks at the cupboard during weekday 9-17h and found it empty every time, and the object's two positive sightings both fall outside that window (03:00, 18:00). By contrast, Marco's vitamins are *found* at the counter twice during 9-17h, meaning they stay home. The journal is at the bedroom desk at 12:00 (two sightings) and back on the nightstand by 18:00, while Marco is at work—so it never leaves.

This document differs from p_b7c2 (which sends the journal and vitamins out with Marco) and from p_a3f1 (which keeps the lunchbox in the cupboard). It predicts the lunchbox is absent from the house 13:40–23:00 on weekdays, the vitamins are on the kitchen counter at midday, and the journal cycles between the desk (midday) and the nightstand (morning and evening). What would refute it: a sighting of the lunchbox inside the house between 14:00 and 22:00 on a weekday, or the vitamins out of the house during that window, or the journal at the desk after 14:00 (when Marco is gone).

